== BLOCKER 1: does the digest need `git`? ==
  'git' appears in checks/substrate-id.py : 1 times (check below)
  `differ.py:58-60` reason, verbatim:
    # documented edit -- a `GCMP_REPO` default in its first `cd`, so the copy can be run from
    # anywhere -- and pinning the copy is what detects the copy drifting. Pinning the committed body
    # instead would be a check against `git`, which is a dependency this file does not otherwise have.
    ORACLE_PIN = {
  -> a sha256 over (relpath, bytes) calls hashlib and pathlib and nothing else, so the
     dependency `differ.py` declines is one this row never takes.  NOT HIT.

== BLOCKER 2: is an mtime clone-dependent and a sha clone-independent? ==
  mtime is st_mtime: a fresh `git clone` of the SAME commit yields a different number on
  every file, because the clone is written now. A sha256 over content is a function of the
  BYTES, so two clones of one commit agree and one clone at two commits does not.
  clone A digest            : 1c51d9ae19e50129  (3 inputs)
  clone A again             : 1c51d9ae19e50129  -> STABLE
  clone A after os.utime()  : 1c51d9ae19e50129  -> UNCHANGED
  and those 3 file(s) now span 0.0 s of mtime, which is what
  an mtime rule would have had to compare and this digest never has to.
  NOT HIT -- and this is the one blocker a sha is strictly BETTER than an mtime on.

